# Suite-wide GAP5 preamble. Reuses the difftest corpus — each case is a
# re-runnable `fn () { ... }` thunk — as an absolute inflated-RC oracle.
#
# Run under CULEBRA_GC_NEVER=1 CULEBRA_GC_LEAK_ABORT=1: the backstop is off (so
# an RC leak is not reclaimed) and the teardown quiescent-point audit aborts if
# any object survives with an inflated refcount (a phantom +1 = an acyclic RC
# leak). Unlike the growth-based leak.sh, this runs the thunk even when it
# THROWS, so it measures the throw-path leaks the growth gate structurally
# skips (its `_p` drops any case whose warmup call throws).
#
# The audit rides the conservative stack scan (best-effort), which can alias a
# lone stranded object as live and under-report it. Running the thunk a handful
# of times accumulates the per-call leak into several stranded objects, so the
# scan can't alias them all — the abort becomes deterministic (a single call is
# marginal and flaky; the 8th run below is well past the knee). Each result is
# discarded to nil: a bare `thunk()` tail expression would return the heap
# result up through `_p` to the discarded top-level `_p(...)`, minting a phantom
# +1 on every heap-returning case (a scan artifact, not a real leak).
fn _p(label, thunk) {
  mut i = 0
  while i < 8 {
    try {
      thunk()
      nil
    } catch e {
      nil
    }
    i = i + 1
  }
  nil
}
